# atomic sandbox replay v1
# M2 "Place adds a nucleus on the focus plane" and the M6 promise "build water from an O and two
# H": from the H atom preset (its H at the origin), the Place tool puts an O 1.81 Bohr to the H's
# right on the default camera's focus plane, then a second H 1.81 Bohr from the O at 104.5
# degrees, at (1.4939, 0, -1.0220) and (1.5286, 1.6461, -1.7738) Bohr. After the solves and the
# free-atom references (O takes about a minute) the density shows two O-H bonds and no H-H one,
# and the molecule is named water.
view 1400 900
action smooth-motion false
action preset h
wait idle
action tool place
action element 8
t 1000 cursor 0.2772541 0
t 1010 button left down
t 1080 button left up
wait idle
action element 1
t 2000 cursor 0.3466729 -0.268423
t 2010 button left down
t 2080 button left up
wait idle
expect nuclei 3
expect dist 0 1 1.80 1.82
expect dist 1 2 1.80 1.82
expect bonds 2
expect molecule 0 H2O
expect no-error
